        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is Sunny Health & Fitness a good treadmill brand?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For walking and light jogging on a budget, yes, provided you buy on figures that Sunny and an independent source agree on. Sunny has sold fitness equipment since 2002, runs its own US store and support line and publishes parts, but quotes motors only in peak horsepower and gives a short warranty on everything except the frame.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the difference between the Sunny SF-T4400 and SF-T4400SMART?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The SF-T4400SMART is the current version, with Bluetooth for the SunnyFit app and a stated 285 lb capacity. The original SF-T4400 has the same 2.2 peak HP motor, 9 mph top speed and three manual incline levels, but a 220 lb limit and no app connection. Sunny’s own store sold only the SMART version on 5 November 2026.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Sunny SF-T7603 discontinued?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It appears so. Its product page on Sunny’s store returned page not found on 5 November 2026, and it appears in Sunny’s parts catalogue only as a model that parts fit. Buy one only used or as old stock, and plan on its 220 lb limit.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty do Sunny treadmills have?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sunny’s warranty policy gives treadmills three years on the frame, one year on the motor and 180 days on other parts, excluding labour and shipping. Product pages list only the frame and 180-day parts terms, so confirm the motor term with Sunny. The warranty covers the original purchaser only, for household use in the US.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can I return a Sunny treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Orders from Sunny’s own website can be returned within 30 days if unused and unopened, in original packaging. For a change of mind you pay return shipping and a 15% restocking fee, plus $200 for freight-shipped items. Purchases from Amazon or other retailers follow that retailer’s policy.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Has Sunny Health & Fitness had a treadmill recall?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. We found no CPSC recall of any Sunny Health & Fitness product when we searched the database on 5 November 2026.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
